    stitch_mcp_file_not_defined_and_missing_auth_2026-09-15, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4-61127: faithful repro of both halves: (1) the doc's exact spawn (bash -lc ... exec npx -y @_davideast/stitch-mcp proxy, shell:false) reaches StitchProxy requires an API key (STITCH_API_KEY or STITCH_ACCESS_TOKEN), exit 1 - the auth gap reproduced verbatim (~/.security/env.sh absent on this host); (2) the import crash: npx content-addresses its cache - _npx/829c6278c197c365 is the same id as the doc's crash path, so the exact bundle is local; emulating the pre-node-20 global surface (delete globalThis.File - File became global in Node 20.0.0) and requiring dist/chunk-spbm03bj.js reproduces ReferenceError: File is not defined at webidl.is.File = webidl.util.MakeTypeAssertion(File) (dist/chunk-spbm03bj.js:12031, @_davideast/stitch-mcp@0.9.0) - a third-party npm package evaluating a bare global at module top level under the older node the Kimi-spawned login shell resolved. Why no in-repo fix: no stitch MCP module exists in src/app or src/lib (exhaustive grep/find/git-log -S stitch-mcp); the only in-repo artifact was a .mcp.json entry launching the external npx package, removed 2026-09-24 by owner request (e760181d7dc, stitch needs a personal API key and fails to connect for everyone else); current tree has no stitch entry in .mcp.json or .kimi-code/mcp.json; the doc's Round-8 (2026-11-06) and Triage (2026-11-13) notes conclude Not a repo defect on this tree - fabricating a module/spec or resurrecting the owner-deleted entry would violate the doc's authority and the no-placeholder spec gate. Verification: neighbouring test/03_system/check/mcp_config_declared_command_launchable_spec 6 examples 4 passed / 2 failed - both failures are the spipe entry only (.spipe/spipe git submodule uninitialized in this worktree, pre-existing environment condition), the 3 config/spelling examples passed. Residuals: the bug remains host-side; doc-documented workarounds (pin absolute node path in the bash snippet, clear the stale _npx cache, record STITCH_API_KEY/STITCH_ACCESS_TOKEN in ~/.security/env.sh mode 600); the upstream package should guard File (polyfill from node:buffer) - an upstream issue, not actionable in-repo. close_evidence reproducer=doc/08_tracking/bug/stitch_mcp_file_not_defined_and_missing_auth_2026-09-15.md prevention=test/03_system/check/mcp_config_declared_command_launchable_spec.spl"
    stitch_mcp_file_not_defined_and_missing_auth_2026-09-15, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: faithful repro of both halves - the doc's exact spawn reaches StitchProxy requires an API key exit 1 (auth gap verbatim, ~/.security/env.sh absent), and the exact npx bundle (content-addressed _npx/829c6278c197c365, same id as the doc's crash path) reproduces ReferenceError: File is not defined at dist/chunk-spbm03bj.js:12031 under an emulated pre-node-20 global surface (File became global in Node 20). No stitch MCP module exists in src (exhaustive search); the only in-repo artifact was a .mcp.json entry removed 2026-09-24 by owner request (e760181d7dc); the doc's Round-8 and Triage notes conclude Not a repo defect. Neighbour mcp_config_declared_command_launchable 4/6 (2 failures are the uninitialized .spipe/spipe submodule, pre-existing). Residuals: host-side workarounds documented in the doc (pin absolute node path, clear the stale npx cache, record STITCH_API_KEY/STITCH_ACCESS_TOKEN in ~/.security/env.sh mode 600); upstream package should guard File. close_evidence reproducer=doc/08_tracking/bug/stitch_mcp_file_not_defined_and_missing_auth_2026-09-15.md prevention=test/03_system/check/mcp_config_declared_command_launchable_spec.spl"

